RunInfo: >
  Requires explicit zero-polarization 160 GeV mu+ p and mu+ n samples, with
  POSNLO and NEGNLO generated separately.
NumEvents: 100000
NeedsCrossSection: yes
Beams: [[ANTIMUON, PROTON], [ANTIMUON, NEUTRON]]
Energies: [[160.0, 0.938272], [160.0, 0.939565]]
Description: >
  Fills charged-kaon numerators, matching inclusive-DIS denominators, and
  same-event covariance proxies only in the 309 published sparse (x,y,z)
  cells. The campaign postprocessor forms the proton/neutron isoscalar sum
  before the ratio and divides by the z-bin width. Published radiative and
  diffractive-vector-meson correction columns are retained as provenance and
  are not applied to the truth-level Herwig prediction.
